IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`

-- bgg4-procedure: BGG 4. Kapitel, 5. Abschnitt, Weitere Verfahrensbestimmungen (Art. 102 to 107).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE DATE): JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text
-- says no, tagged FALSE-kind), NOTHING (not covered, tagged NOTHING-kind).  See bgg4-appealable
-- for the key.  A function named for a power ("may") whose gate fails answers NOTHING, with one
-- fork line (the ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1).
-- Dates are `Date day month year`; a period of days is the text's own and is inclusive of its
-- last day (see bgg4-time-limit for the day count).

§ `Art 102 Schriftenwechsel (exchange of submissions)`

-- src:83 | 1 Soweit erforderlich stellt das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde der Vorinstanz sowie den allfälligen anderen Parteien, Beteiligten oder zur Beschwerde berechtigten Behörden zu und setzt ihnen Frist zur Einreichung einer Vernehmlassung an.
@ref Art. 102(1) BGG (src:83)
GIVEN `service of the appeal on this recipient is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN                                                   -- soweit erforderlich: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
      `the recipient is the lower instance, another party, a participant or an authority entitled to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN   -- die Vorinstanz sowie die allfälligen anderen Parteien, Beteiligten oder zur Beschwerde berechtigten Behörden
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 102(1) the Federal Supreme Court must serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` MEANS
    IF `service of the appeal on this recipient is necessary` AND `the recipient is the lower instance, another party, a participant or an authority entitled to appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Soweit erforderlich" limits the duty to what is necessary and names the recipients; outside the limit the paragraph says nothing

-- The Court's duty, as a regulative rule.  No time limit is stated for it and none is invented.
-- src:83 | 1 Soweit erforderlich stellt das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde der Vorinstanz sowie den allfälligen anderen Parteien, Beteiligten oder zur Beschwerde berechtigten Behörden zu und setzt ihnen Frist zur Einreichung einer Vernehmlassung an.
@ref Art. 102(1) BGG (the duty) (src:83)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 102(1) the Court's duty to serve the appeal and set a time limit` MEANS
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court`
    MUST `serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations`

-- src:84 | 2 Die Vorinstanz hat innert dieser Frist die Vorakten einzusenden.
@ref Art. 102(2) BGG (src:84)
GIVEN `the last day of the time limit set under paragraph 1` IS A DATE          -- "innert dieser Frist": the Court sets the time limit (the text does not give its length)
      `the day the lower instance sent the files` IS A DATE                     -- Vorakten
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 102(2) the lower instance has sent the files within the time limit` MEANS
    IF `the day the lower instance sent the files` AT MOST `the last day of the time limit set under paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Die Vorinstanz hat innert dieser Frist die Vorakten einzusenden." (a period the text fixes by reference to the Court's time limit: outside it, JUST FALSE under periods ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)

-- The lower instance's duty, as a regulative rule.  The length of the time limit is set by the Court and is an input.
-- src:84 | 2 Die Vorinstanz hat innert dieser Frist die Vorakten einzusenden.
@ref Art. 102(2) BGG (the duty) (src:84)
GIVEN `the length of the time limit set under paragraph 1, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 102(2) the lower instance's duty to send the files within the time limit` MEANS
    PARTY `Lower instance`
    MUST `send the files to the Federal Supreme Court`
    WITHIN `the length of the time limit set under paragraph 1, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Lower instance` BECAUSE "the files were not sent within the time limit the Court set"

-- src:85 | 3 Ein weiterer Schriftenwechsel findet in der Regel nicht statt.
@ref Art. 102(3) BGG (src:85)
GIVEN `the case is an exception to the rule that no further exchange of submissions takes place` IS A BOOLEAN        -- "in der Regel": the text names no exception
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 102(3) a further exchange of submissions takes place` MEANS
    IF `the case is an exception to the rule that no further exchange of submissions takes place`
    THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in der Regel" leaves exceptions open and the paragraph names none (fork F14)
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Ein weiterer Schriftenwechsel findet in der Regel nicht statt."

§ `Art 103 Aufschiebende Wirkung (suspensive effect)`

-- src:88 | 1 Die Beschwerde hat in der Regel keine aufschiebende Wirkung.
@ref Art. 103(1) BGG (src:88)
GIVEN `an exception to the rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- paragraphs 2 and 3 name exceptions
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(1) the appeal has suspensive effect` MEANS
    IF `an exception to the rule applies`
    THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in der Regel" leaves exceptions open; paragraphs 2 and 3 give them
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Die Beschwerde hat in der Regel keine aufschiebende Wirkung."

-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:90 | a. in Zivilsachen, wenn sie sich gegen ein Gestaltungsurteil richtet;
@ref Art. 103(2)(a) BGG (src:89-90)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` IS A BOOLEAN            -- Gestaltungsurteil
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (kind EQUALS `appeal in civil matters`) THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (a) reaches only "Zivilsachen"
        IF `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in Zivilsachen, wenn sie sich gegen ein Gestaltungsurteil richtet" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F15)

-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:91 | b. in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen einen Entscheid richtet, der eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme ausspricht; die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche;
@ref Art. 103(2)(b) BGG (src:89) (src:91)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` IS A BOOLEAN       -- eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme
      `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- der Entscheid über Zivilansprüche
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (kind EQUALS `appeal in criminal matters`) THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (b) reaches only "Strafsachen"
        IF `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche"
        IF `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen einen Entscheid richtet, der eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme ausspricht" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F15)

-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:92 | c. in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen eine Schlussverfügung oder gegen jede andere Verfügung richtet, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt;
@ref Art. 103(2)(c) BGG (src:89) (src:92)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- Schlussverfügung
      `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` IS A BOOLEAN   -- jede andere Verfügung, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (c) reaches only proceedings "auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen"
        IF `the appeal is against a final order` OR `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn sie sich gegen eine Schlussverfügung oder gegen jede andere Verfügung richtet, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F15)

-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:93 | d.[^10] in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen.
@ref Art. 103(2)(d) BGG (src:89) (src:93)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(2)(d) the appeal has suspensive effect in international administrative assistance in tax matters` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (d) reaches only "Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen"

-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:90 | a. in Zivilsachen, wenn sie sich gegen ein Gestaltungsurteil richtet;
-- src:91 | b. in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen einen Entscheid richtet, der eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme ausspricht; die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche;
-- src:92 | c. in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen eine Schlussverfügung oder gegen jede andere Verfügung richtet, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt;
-- src:93 | d.[^10] in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen.
@ref Art. 103(2) BGG (src:89-93)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` kind `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` kind `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 103(2)(d) the appeal has suspensive effect in international administrative assistance in tax matters` `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE          -- "im Umfang der Begehren": to the extent of the claims, which the person states as a yes or no (fork F16)
        IF     `Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` kind `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            OR `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` kind `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            OR `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "wenn" of limb (a), (b) or (c) failed, or "die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche" (limb (b))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no limb of paragraph 2 reaches the case

-- src:94 | 3 Der Instruktionsrichter oder die Instruktionsrichterin kann über die aufschiebende Wirkung von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei eine andere Anordnung treffen.
@ref Art. 103(3) BGG (src:94)
GIVEN `the order concerns the suspensive effect of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                                           -- über die aufschiebende Wirkung
      `the order is made on the judge's own motion or on a party's request` IS A BOOLEAN                              -- von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103(3) the instructing judge may make a different order on suspensive effect` MEANS
    IF `the order concerns the suspensive effect of the appeal` AND `the order is made on the judge's own motion or on a party's request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("kann ... eine andere Anordnung treffen") whose stated gate failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

-- Paragraphs (1) to (3) together.  The instructing judge's order, where one was made, governs; otherwise paragraph 2, and where
-- no limb of paragraph 2 reaches the case, the rule of paragraph 1.
-- src:88 | 1 Die Beschwerde hat in der Regel keine aufschiebende Wirkung.
-- src:89 | 2 Die Beschwerde hat im Umfang der Begehren aufschiebende Wirkung:
-- src:90 | a. in Zivilsachen, wenn sie sich gegen ein Gestaltungsurteil richtet;
-- src:91 | b. in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen einen Entscheid richtet, der eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme ausspricht; die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche;
-- src:92 | c. in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen eine Schlussverfügung oder gegen jede andere Verfügung richtet, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt;
-- src:93 | d.[^10] in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen.
-- src:94 | 3 Der Instruktionsrichter oder die Instruktionsrichterin kann über die aufschiebende Wirkung von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei eine andere Anordnung treffen.
@ref Art. 103 BGG (src:88-94)
GIVEN order IS A `Order on suspensive effect`
      kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `the instructing judge ordered that the appeal has suspensive effect` THEN JUST TRUE         -- "eine andere Anordnung treffen": the order governs (Art 103(3))
    WHEN `the instructing judge ordered that the appeal has no suspensive effect` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "kann über die aufschiebende Wirkung ... eine andere Anordnung treffen": the order governs (Art 103(3); the person states what was ordered)
    WHEN `the instructing judge made no order on suspensive effect` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` kind `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            IF `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` kind `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 2's "wenn" failed, or "erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche"; and "in der Regel keine aufschiebende Wirkung" (paragraph 1)
            OTHERWISE `Art 103(1) the appeal has suspensive effect` FALSE

§ `Art 104 Andere vorsorgliche Massnahmen (other provisional measures)`

-- src:97 | Der Instruktionsrichter oder die Instruktionsrichterin kann von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei vorsorgliche Massnahmen treffen, um den bestehenden Zustand zu erhalten oder bedrohte Interessen einstweilen sicherzustellen.
@ref Art. 104 BGG (src:97)
GIVEN `the measure is ordered on the judge's own motion or on a party's request` IS A BOOLEAN                        -- von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei
      `the measure serves to preserve the existing state of affairs or to secure threatened interests for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN   -- um den bestehenden Zustand zu erhalten oder bedrohte Interessen einstweilen sicherzustellen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure` MEANS
    IF `the measure is ordered on the judge's own motion or on a party's request` AND `the measure serves to preserve the existing state of affairs or to secure threatened interests for the time being`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("kann ... vorsorgliche Massnahmen treffen") whose stated purpose or trigger is not met answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

§ `Art 105 Massgebender Sachverhalt (the facts that count)`

-- src:100 | 1 Das Bundesgericht legt seinem Urteil den Sachverhalt zugrunde, den die Vorinstanz festgestellt hat.
@ref Art. 105(1) BGG (src:100)
GIVEN `the facts were found by the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 105(1) the Court bases its judgment on the facts found by the lower instance` MEANS
    IF `the facts were found by the lower instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "den Sachverhalt zugrunde, den die Vorinstanz festgestellt hat"; of facts the lower instance did not find it says nothing

-- src:101 | 2 Es kann die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz von Amtes wegen berichtigen oder ergänzen, wenn sie offensichtlich unrichtig ist oder auf einer Rechtsverletzung im Sinne von Artikel 95 beruht.
@ref Art. 105(2) BGG (src:101)
GIVEN `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN                                                  -- offensichtlich unrichtig
      `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` IS A BOOLEAN           -- auf einer Rechtsverletzung im Sinne von Artikel 95 beruht
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` MEANS
    IF `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` OR `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("kann ... von Amtes wegen berichtigen oder ergänzen") whose "wenn" gate failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

-- src:102 | 3 Richtet sich die Beschwerde gegen einen Entscheid über die Zusprechung oder Verweigerung von Geldleistungen der Militär- oder Unfallversicherung, so ist das Bundesgericht nicht an die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz gebunden.[^11]
@ref Art. 105(3) BGG (src:102)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 105(3) the Court is bound by the finding of the facts` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance`
    THEN JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so ist das Bundesgericht nicht an die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz gebunden"
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only "Geldleistungen der Militär- oder Unfallversicherung"; for any other appeal this paragraph is silent

-- src:100 | 1 Das Bundesgericht legt seinem Urteil den Sachverhalt zugrunde, den die Vorinstanz festgestellt hat.
-- src:101 | 2 Es kann die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz von Amtes wegen berichtigen oder ergänzen, wenn sie offensichtlich unrichtig ist oder auf einer Rechtsverletzung im Sinne von Artikel 95 beruht.
-- src:102 | 3 Richtet sich die Beschwerde gegen einen Entscheid über die Zusprechung oder Verweigerung von Geldleistungen der Militär- oder Unfallversicherung, so ist das Bundesgericht nicht an die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz gebunden.[^11]
@ref Art. 105 BGG (src:100-102)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facts were found by the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 105(3) the Court is bound by the finding of the facts` `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so ist das Bundesgericht nicht an die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz gebunden"
        IF `Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2 gives the Court a power ("kann") to correct or supplement; the text does not say it must, so it neither says "bound" nor "not bound" (fork F18)
        IF `Art 105(1) the Court bases its judgment on the facts found by the lower instance` `the facts were found by the lower instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 speaks of the facts the lower instance found

§ `Art 106 Rechtsanwendung (application of the law)`

-- src:105 | 1 Das Bundesgericht wendet das Recht von Amtes wegen an.
@ref Art. 106(1) BGG (src:105)
GIVEN rule IS A `Kind of rule in Art 106`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 106(1) the Court applies the rule of its own motion` MEANS
    IF rule EQUALS `other law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 states the general rule and paragraph 2 limits it for fundamental rights and for cantonal and intercantonal law; for those the sentence itself does not say no (fork F19)

-- src:106 | 2 Es prüft die Verletzung von Grundrechten und von kantonalem und interkantonalem Recht nur insofern, als eine solche Rüge in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden ist.
@ref Art. 106(2) BGG (src:106)
GIVEN rule IS A `Kind of rule in Art 106`
      `the complaint was raised in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- vorgebracht
      `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- begründet
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF rule EQUALS `other law` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2 reaches only "Grundrechten und ... kantonalem und interkantonalem Recht"
        IF `the complaint was raised in the appeal` AND `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nur insofern, als eine solche Rüge in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden ist"

-- src:105 | 1 Das Bundesgericht wendet das Recht von Amtes wegen an.
-- src:106 | 2 Es prüft die Verletzung von Grundrechten und von kantonalem und interkantonalem Recht nur insofern, als eine solche Rüge in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden ist.
@ref Art. 106 BGG (src:105-106)
GIVEN rule IS A `Kind of rule in Art 106`
      `the complaint was raised in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 106 the Court examines the violation of the rule` MEANS
    IF rule EQUALS `other law`
    THEN `Art 106(1) the Court applies the rule of its own motion` rule
    ELSE `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` rule `the complaint was raised in the appeal` `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal`

§ `Art 107 Entscheid (decision)`

-- An unconditional flat negative: "darf nicht ... hinausgehen" carries no condition and no limit of its own, so the standing question
-- "may the Court go beyond the parties' claims?" needs no fact and is answered JUST FALSE (fork F33).
-- src:109 | 1 Das Bundesgericht darf nicht über die Begehren der Parteien hinausgehen.
@ref Art. 107(1) BGG (src:109)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 107(1) the Court is permitted to go beyond the claims of the parties` MEANS
    JUST FALSE              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Das Bundesgericht darf nicht über die Begehren der Parteien hinausgehen."

-- src:110 | 2 Heisst das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde gut, so entscheidet es in der Sache selbst oder weist diese zu neuer Beurteilung an die Vorinstanz zurück. Es kann die Sache auch an die Behörde zurückweisen, die als erste Instanz entschieden hat.
@ref Art. 107(2) BGG (src:110)
GIVEN `the Court upholds the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- heisst die Beschwerde gut
      outcome IS A `Outcome of an upheld appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Court upholds the appeal` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Heisst das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde gut" limits the paragraph to an upheld appeal
        IF outcome EQUALS `the Court decides the matter itself` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF outcome EQUALS `the Court remits the matter to the lower instance for a new judgment` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF outcome EQUALS `the Court remits the matter to the authority that decided as first instance` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names three outcomes and does not close the list with "nur"

-- Paragraph (3), first sentence: the 15 days.
-- src:111 | 3 Erachtet das Bundesgericht eine Beschwerde auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen oder der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen als unzulässig, so fällt es den Nichteintretensentscheid innert 15 Tagen seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels. Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt.[^12]
@ref Art. 107(3) BGG (first sentence) (src:111)
GIVEN `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN                                        -- als unzulässig erachtet
      `an exchange of submissions took place` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- allfälliger Schriftenwechsel
      `the day the exchange of submissions ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` OR `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches only appeals "auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen oder der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen"
        IF NOT `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` THEN NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches only an appeal the Court "Erachtet das Bundesgericht eine Beschwerde ... als unzulässig"
        IF NOT `an exchange of submissions took place` THEN NOTHING                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 15 days run "seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels" and the text gives no start where there was none (fork F20)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the day the exchange of submissions ended` PLUS 15)

-- Paragraph (3), second sentence: no 15 days for extradition where the asylum application has no final decision.
-- src:111 | 3 Erachtet das Bundesgericht eine Beschwerde auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen oder der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen als unzulässig, so fällt es den Nichteintretensentscheid innert 15 Tagen seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels. Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt.[^12]
@ref Art. 107(3) BGG (second sentence) (src:111)
GIVEN `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force` IS A BOOLEAN   -- gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the second sentence reaches only "Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen"; for tax assistance the first sentence alone speaks and this function is not asked about it
        IF `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force` THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE     -- the first sentence gives the 15 days as the rule for this field and this exception is the only limit the second sentence states; it is introduced with "wenn" and is not made out, so the text's own words leave the Court bound (fork F34)

-- src:111 | 3 Erachtet das Bundesgericht eine Beschwerde auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen oder der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen als unzulässig, so fällt es den Nichteintretensentscheid innert 15 Tagen seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels. Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt.[^12]
@ref Art. 107(3) BGG (the decision is within the period) (src:111)
GIVEN `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exchange of submissions took place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the exchange of submissions ended` IS A DATE
      `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision not to enter was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): where the Court "nicht an diese Frist gebunden" is, the period is not the test
        IF `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` `an exchange of submissions took place` `the day the exchange of submissions ended` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter
        IF `the day the decision not to enter was given` AT MOST (fromMaybe `the day the exchange of submissions ended` (`Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` `an exchange of submissions took place` `the day the exchange of submissions ended`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so fällt es den Nichteintretensentscheid innert 15 Tagen seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels" (a period the text fixes in its own words: periods ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)

-- src:111 | 3 Erachtet das Bundesgericht eine Beschwerde auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen oder der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen als unzulässig, so fällt es den Nichteintretensentscheid innert 15 Tagen seit Abschluss eines allfälligen Schriftenwechsels. Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt.[^12]
@ref Art. 107(3) BGG (the duty) (src:111)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 107(3) the Court's duty to give the decision not to enter within 15 days` MEANS
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court`
    MUST `give the decision not to enter on the appeal`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Federal Supreme Court` BECAUSE "the decision not to enter was not given within 15 days after the end of the exchange of submissions"

-- Paragraph (4): one month.  A month is not a count of days: the last day is the same day of the following month, and
-- where the following month has no such day the text states no rule, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F21).
-- src:112 | 4 Über Beschwerden gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts über die Erteilung einer Lizenz nach Artikel 40d des Patentgesetzes vom 25. Juni 1954[^13] entscheidet das Bundesgericht innerhalb eines Monats nach Anhebung der Beschwerde.[^14]
@ref Art. 107(4) BGG (src:112)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the appeal was brought` IS A DATE                                   -- Anhebung der Beschwerde
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only "Beschwerden gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts über die Erteilung einer Lizenz nach Artikel 40d des Patentgesetzes"
        IF DATE_DAY (`add months` `the day the appeal was brought` 1) EQUALS DATE_DAY `the day the appeal was brought` THEN JUST (`add months` `the day the appeal was brought` 1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no rule for a following month that has no such day

-- src:112 | 4 Über Beschwerden gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts über die Erteilung einer Lizenz nach Artikel 40d des Patentgesetzes vom 25. Juni 1954[^13] entscheidet das Bundesgericht innerhalb eines Monats nach Anhebung der Beschwerde.[^14]
@ref Art. 107(4) BGG (the decision is within one month) (src:112)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the appeal was brought` IS A DATE
      `the day the Court decided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` `the day the appeal was brought`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF `the day the Court decided` AT MOST lastDay
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "entscheidet das Bundesgericht innerhalb eines Monats nach Anhebung der Beschwerde" (a period the text fixes in its own words: periods ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The duty of paragraph (4) as a regulative rule.  A month is not a fixed number of days, so the number of days from the day
-- the appeal was brought to the same day of the following month is an input.
-- src:112 | 4 Über Beschwerden gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts über die Erteilung einer Lizenz nach Artikel 40d des Patentgesetzes vom 25. Juni 1954[^13] entscheidet das Bundesgericht innerhalb eines Monats nach Anhebung der Beschwerde.[^14]
@ref Art. 107(4) BGG (the duty) (src:112)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the appeal was brought to the same day of the following month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 107(4) the Court's duty to decide within one month` MEANS
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court`
    MUST `decide on the appeal against the Federal Patent Court decision on a licence`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day the appeal was brought to the same day of the following month`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Federal Supreme Court` BECAUSE "the Court did not decide within one month after the appeal was brought"
